From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:47:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 52/56] LibWeb: removing the focused element makes the viewport
 the focused area (HTML removing steps 1-2)

Before, the removed element stayed the document's focused area: activeElement answered it and the next focus event named it as relatedTarget, where Chrome gives null.
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLElement.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLElement.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLElement.cpp
index 0346456088..6bc9de7bf1 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLElement.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLElement.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 #include <LibWeb/HTML/PopoverTargetAttributes.h>
 #include <LibWeb/HTML/Scripting/Environments.h>
 #include <LibWeb/HTML/ToggleEvent.h>
+#include <LibWeb/HTML/Navigation.h>
 #include <LibWeb/HTML/Window.h>
 #include <LibWeb/HighResolutionTime/TimeOrigin.h>
 #include <LibWeb/Layout/Box.h>
@@ -2213,9 +2214,18 @@ void HTMLElement::removed_from(IsSubtreeRoot is_subtree_root, Node* old_ancestor
 {
     Element::removed_from(is_subtree_root, old_ancestor, old_root);
 
-    // FIXME: 1. Let document be removedNode's node document.
-    // FIXME: 2. If document's focused area is removedNode, then set document's focused area to document's viewport,
+    // 1. Let document be removedNode's node document.
+    auto& node_document = document();
+
+    // 2. If document's focused area is removedNode, then set document's focused area to document's viewport,
     //   and set document's relevant global object's navigation API's focus changed during ongoing navigation to false.
+    // NB: A null focused area is the viewport. Without this the removed element stayed the focused area: activeElement
+    //     answered it and the next focus event named it as its relatedTarget, where Chrome gives null.
+    if (node_document.focused_area().ptr() == this) {
+        node_document.set_focused_area(nullptr);
+        if (auto window = node_document.window())
+            window->navigation()->set_focus_changed_during_ongoing_navigation(false);
+    }
 
     // 3. If removedNode is an element whose namespace is the HTML namespace, and this standard defines HTML element
     //    removing steps for removedNode's local name, then run the corresponding HTML element removing steps given
-- 
